# MediMate AI – Frontend Environment Configuration
# HacXLerate 2026 Production & Local Setup

# Backend API Base URL
#
# Local Development:
# Leave empty to use the Vite proxy configured in vite.config.ts (http://127.0.0.1:8000),
# or explicitly set to: http://localhost:8000
#
# Production Deployment (e.g., Render, Railway, Fly.io):
# Set this to the public URL of your deployed backend service.
# Example: VITE_API_URL="https://your-medimate-backend.onrender.com"
# Note: You can include or omit trailing slashes and '/api' - api.ts automatically normalizes it.
VITE_API_URL=""
